#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
FOLLOW-UP ANALYSIS (optimized):
Count Synaptophysin and PSD95 puncta around already segmented NeuN-positive cells.
Updated to support Signed Distance Shells (negative values for inner shell limits).

RESUME SUPPORT:
    If SKIP_IF_OUTPUT_EXISTS is True (default), a file is skipped when its
    QC projection PNG (<image_stem>_puncta_QC.png) already exists in the
    output folder -- that PNG is the last thing analyze_one_image() writes,
    so its presence means that file completed successfully on a previous
    run. This lets you re-run the whole batch after an interruption/crash
    without redoing already-finished files. Set SKIP_IF_OUTPUT_EXISTS to
    False to force reprocessing of every file (e.g. after changing
    detection parameters).

    Skipped files' per-cell/summary rows are NOT lost: at the end of the
    run, any existing all_images_per_neun_cell.csv / all_images_sample_
    summary.csv already in OUTPUT_ROOT (from a previous run) are loaded
    and merged with whatever was newly processed this run (see
    merge_with_existing_csv()). If the same file_name appears in both the
    old CSV and this run's results, the NEW result wins (so re-running a
    file with different parameters correctly overwrites its old row
    rather than duplicating it).
"""

